      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 825735594,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "@rknall - Can you (and any other Qt experts in the house) validate this MR's approach for resolving the crash reported in #17789 (and #17819)? These crashes appear to be triggered by a thread context and/or reparenting problem.\n\nThe \"object\" addresses reported in the log messages of the macOS console crash reports (e.g. \"Wireshark(40316,0x103e7bd40) malloc: *** error for object 0x16ce4d190: pointer being freed was not allocated\"),  appears to be the address of the QFileDialog object. When the file_dialog_button_ does NOT have focus when the WiresharkFileDialog method is called, the QFileDialog appears to be assigned as the parent of the EditorFileDialog. In this case the EditorFileDialog appears to be destructed prematurely.\n\nWhile investigating the crash I sprinkled copious qDebug() throughput the UatDialog, EditorFileDialog, and WiresharkFileDialog modules watching the `this` and `this->parent()` objects with QObject's dumpObjectTree() and dumpObjectInfo() methods. I also added some destructors where none existed hoping for more insight. The debugging reports ultimately led to this patch.\n\nWhile this patch appears to avoid the parenting/premature_destroy crash issue I don't think this is the final word.\n\nWhy should this patch be necessary for macOS? Could the true root cause of these crashes be something like a misuse of the Qt API on our part or worse yet an actual regression in Qt's macOS implementation?\n\nAccurately answering these last set of questions is above my (current) skillset.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6682068,
            "username": "jim.young",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Jim Young",
            "state": "active",
